    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The cosmos was divided into hanan pacha above, kay pacha where humans live and ukhu pacha and urin pacha within the earth, represented by the condor, the puma and the snake.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> allowed conquered peoples to keep their own deities while making the cult of the Sun the official tradition of the empire.</li><li>Royal ancestors were mummified and consulted as advisors, and in times of great trouble the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> practised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/human-sacrifice">human sacrifice</a>, usually of a child (qhapaq hucha) or a slave.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> valley held 328 huacas, which were arranged along 41 or 42 radial pathways called ceques, all running out from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coricancha">Coricancha</a>, and the ritual duties for each shrine were recorded on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quipu">quipus</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

