    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">13th century</span><span class="rf-text">In the early 1200s the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> form the small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/city-state">city-state</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cuzco</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manco-capac">Manco Capac</a>, who builds a temple to the Sun God, called Inticancha, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coricancha">Coricancha</a> stands</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1438</span><span class="rf-text">Under the ninth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sapa-inca">Sapa Inca</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pachacuti">Pachacuti</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> begin the expansion that brings much of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> into the empire, with the cult of the Sun as its official tradition</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1527</span><span class="rf-text">As many as 4,000 servants, court officials, favourites and concubines are killed on the death of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huayna-capac">Huayna Capac</a>, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/human-sacrifice">human sacrifices</a> the Inca made</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1532</span><span class="rf-text">The Spanish begin the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>, and on their arrival the Inca begin to hide the bodies of their kings and worship more secretly</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1559</span><span class="rf-text">Polo de Ondegardo, newly appointed Corregidor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cuzco</a>, hunts down the mummies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> kings and sends them to the viceroy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1564</span><span class="rf-text">The Taki Unquy movement arises in Huamanga, in the Peruvian Andes, calling for a return to the worship of the huacas and a rejection of the Christian god</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1572</span><span class="rf-text">The last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> stronghold is conquered, and the Taki Unquy practice is estimated to have ended in the same year</span></li></ol>
    </section>

